  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive ({他動詞|たどうし}). Takes を for what is scattered or who is shaken off.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{撒|ま}いている describes an ongoing scattering action.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {水|みず}を{撒|ま}く: to sprinkle water\n- {塩|しお}を{撒|ま}く: to spread salt\n- {豆|まめ}を{撒|ま}く: to scatter beans (Setsubun)\n- {尾行|びこう}を{撒|ま}く: to shake off a tail\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {蒔|ま}く: to sow (seeds, specifically for planting)\n- {撒|ま}く: to scatter, to sprinkle (broader, not necessarily for planting)\n- {巻|ま}く: to wind, to wrap (different kanji and meaning)",
